WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.402
Dates become much more useful after they are converted into a true date-time type.

00:00:05.402 --> 00:00:11.942
Pandas provides a date-time accessor that lets us extract calendar information from a date column.

00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:16.037
In the example, we create month, weekday, and quarter from order date.

00:00:16.037 --> 00:00:23.512
These new columns can support questions such as whether sales are stronger on certain days,

00:00:23.512 --> 00:00:29.087
whether activity changes by month, or how performance compares across quarters.

00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:34.157
Date features are especially useful in reporting and time-based analysis.

00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:40.467
Always confirm that the original date values were parsed correctly before extracting features from them,

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:44.376
because an invalid date can become a missing date during conversion.
